## Edge cases handled

| Scenario                              | Behaviour                                                   |
|---------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| Ticket created before business hours  | Clock starts at 09:00 same day (or next business day).      |
| Ticket created after business hours   | Clock starts at 09:00 next business day.                    |
| Ticket created on weekend/holiday     | Clock starts at 09:00 next business day.                    |
| ON_HOLD at end of timeline            | Clock stops at ON_HOLD entry; never resumes.                |
| Multiple ON_HOLD segments             | Each pause-resume pair handled independently.               |
| Status history out of order           | Automatically sorted chronologically.                       |
| Overlapping status timestamps         | Only positive-duration intervals counted.                   |
| Naive datetimes                       | Treated as UTC.                                             |
| Duplicate holidays                    | Deduplicated.                                               |
| Empty ticket list                     | Summary shows 0 totals, no crash.                           |
| Missing optional fields               | Sensible defaults (`unassigned`, `unknown`).                |
| DST transitions                       | Handled by IANA timezone (pytz/zoneinfo).                   |

